abstract:
This paper provides closed-form formulas for coefficients of convergents of some popular continued fraction expansions (CFEs) approximating <formula formulatype="inline" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><tex Notation="TeX">$s^{
u}$</tex></formula>, with <formula formulatype="inline" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><tex Notation="TeX">$-1&lt;
u&lt;1$</tex></formula>, and <formula formulatype="inline" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><tex Notation="TeX">$(2/T)^{
u}((z-1)/(z+1))^{
u}$</tex> </formula>. The expressions of the coefficients are given in terms of <formula formulatype="inline" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><tex Notation="TeX">$
u$</tex></formula> and of the degree <formula formulatype="inline" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><tex Notation="TeX">$n$</tex></formula> of the polynomials defining the convergents. The formulas greatly reduce the effort for approximating fractional operators and show the equivalence between two well-known CFEs in a given condition.
